# Cursor Rules: Next.js Project Standards

You are working on a Next.js App Router TypeScript project.

## File System Rules
- Put pages/routes in `app/**/page.tsx`.
- Put API endpoints in `app/api/**/route.ts`.
- Put reusable UI in `components/` and primitives in `components/ui/`.
- Put business logic and DB utilities in `lib/`.
- Put shared types in `types/`.
- Put Prisma schema/migrations in `prisma/`.

## Architecture Rules
- Keep API routes thin. Move complex logic to `lib/*-service.ts`.
- Enforce auth and authorization for project-scoped routes.
- Validate request body/params before writes.
- Always scope project resources by `projectId`.
- Keep response/error payloads consistent.

## Frontend Rules
- Reuse existing shadcn patterns (table/dialog/select/badge).
- Keep route pages minimal; compose from `components/pages/*`.
- Preserve `?project=` context in navigation links.
- Prefer clear loading/empty/error states in data-driven UI.

## Data + Migrations
- Update `prisma/schema.prisma` and create migration together.
- Avoid breaking migration changes unless explicitly requested.
- Regenerate Prisma client after schema updates.

## Quality Gates
- Ensure strict TypeScript compatibility.
- Run `npm run build` after significant changes.
- Avoid unrelated refactors in feature PRs.
